# SV-V-LAB6
Task 1: Requirement Extraction
1.1 Functional Requirements (FRs)
Req. ID	Requirement	Type	Priority	Verification Method
FR-01	The system shall initialize each robot in IDLE when switched on.	FR	High	State transition test
FR-02	The robot shall accept a delivery request only after validating the request and destination.	FR	High	Functional test
FR-03	The system shall authenticate an operator and verify their role before accepting a command.	FR	Critical	Security test
FR-04	The robot shall detect obstacles, suspend navigation, avoid the obstacle, and resume its route when safe.	FR	Critical	Simulation test
FR-05	The robot shall deliver a package only after reaching its assigned destination and confirming delivery conditions.	FR	High	Integration test
FR-06	The robot shall abandon its delivery and return to the warehouse when its battery reaches the emergency level.	FR	Critical	Battery fault-injection test
FR-07	The chamber shall check essential sensors at power-on and enable monitoring only if all required sensors pass.	FR	Critical	Sensor fault-injection test
FR-08	The chamber shall load the batch identity and temperature/humidity limits and begin conservation only when the profile is loaded and the door is closed.	FR	Critical	Chamber integration test
FR-09	The chamber shall correct out-of-range temperature or humidity and verify recovery through sensor readings.	FR	Critical	Environmental simulation test
FR-10	The system shall record robot events, command outcomes, chamber faults, and safety incidents with timestamps.	FR	High	Log inspection test
1.2 Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs)
These requirements include proposed measurable targets because the scenario does not specify exact performance limits. They should be approved by the health authority before the baseline is finalized.
Req. ID	Requirement	Type	Priority	Verification Method
NFR-01	The robot shall enter Safe Mode within 3 seconds of detecting a defined critical battery or chamber/battery temperature condition.	NFR / Safety	Critical	Timed fault-injection test
NFR-02	The system shall support at least 20 robots connected to Mission Control simultaneously.	NFR	High	Load test
NFR-03	The system shall reject 100% of commands that lack valid authentication or required role authorization.	NFR / Security	Critical	Penetration and access-control tests
NFR-04	Under the specified pilot workload, 95% of telemetry messages shall be processed within 5 seconds of receipt by Mission Control.	NFR / Performance	High	Performance test
NFR-05	The portal shall provide searchable robot, operator, and project-artefact records, with 95% of searches returning results within 2 seconds under the pilot workload.	NFR / Usability	Medium	Usability and response-time test
Note: The 5-second telemetry and 2-second portal targets are proposed engineering targets, not facts given in the scenario. The low-bandwidth link has delays of several seconds, so end-to-end delivery time must be measured separately.
